{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/983177-interesting-character-ideas","id":983177,"title":"Interesting Character Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-06T23:20:04-07:00","id":983177,"title":"Interesting Character Ideas","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><u><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I noticed a trend of these popping up and decided to try one here.</span></u><br /> <br /> <br /> Frederic Stormeye:</b></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Some might say it is rare for one of the Ithaeur to hold the rank of pack alpha, with usually such a role being delegated to the mightiest warrior, or cleverest hunter. But Frederic Stormeye has proven himself an effective leader by his aptitude for diplomacy. He earned his deed name for the stoic calm he exhibits towards others, like the eye of a storm that offers a reprieve before the assault begins anew. Those who know him personally advise that it is wise to listen to what the shaman has to say. For if diplomacy fails to resolve the issue, his pack will rain down a storm of violence upon their enemies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Frederic underwent the First Change during his middle years of highschool. Tragically during his first sexual encounter with a girl he had been crushing on for a while. She did not survive the experience and Frederic woke up the next morning covered in more than just virgin blood. He was later discovered by the Forsaken, who explained his condition to him and inducted him into Oath of the Moon. As an Ithaeur, Frederic adapted to his new life much quicker than other kids his age. He became fascinated with the world of spirits and devoted his formative years to bargaining for Gifts and studying Rites. The people expected him to petition the Bone Shadows for membership, but he surprised everyone by offering himself to the Storm Lords, instead!<br /> <br /> <br /> During his initiation test, Frederic was tasked with cowling a spirit into submission. The purpose was to test his force of personality and strength. Frederic approached the unruly spirit and began to make peaceful, yet firm negotiations with it. Ultimately, the spirit complied with Frederic's terms without coaxing additional payment out of him. While the Storm Lords were concerned that he offered to pay off the spirit, they decided that the steadfast way he handled the negotiations was passable, and so he was accepted into the tribe.<br /> <br /> <br /> It has been about 10 years now since Frederic underwent the first change. In that time, he has become the alpha of his own pack, which he has named <i>Hurricane Lupus</i> in honor of their destructive ferocity in battle. Each member of his pack is deed named after some manner of weather phenomenon, and he wishes to maintain this theme for new members.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":".  Fixed the Storm Lord spelling. 10-07-2016, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T02:47:51-07:00","id":983230,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm fairly happy with my current character, so I'll throw him in. This is a 1ed game, so maybe some elements are obsolete.<br /> <br /> Jason Sebastian Conrad (no deed name) :<br /> <br /> At 31, Jason was a successful businessman. Born in Grand Rapids, Michigan, he studied in Philadelphia before moving to Lansing where he contributed to building Silver Lining Network, a local independent TV channel, while increasing his wealth. Then, one month, he started feeling more... on edge. He had occasional mood swings at work, but managed to keep it together until one day. He decided to vent some anger at one of his peers' recent decision and went for a jog in a park at night. There stood two men a behind some trees : One, a small time dealer was threatening his &quot;client&quot; who maybe didn't have the money. Jason hid behind a bush and called the police for help, only to be blown off by the officer who took his call. Then, something snapped and all went blank. When Jason came to, he was naked and splattered in blood as body parts were scattered around. One day later, a pack with ties to the police found him and asked him to come so they could explain a few things.<br /> <br /> Since then, he has considered his new condition more a curse than anything. He fears what he has become and nothing can ever undo the two murders he committed, even the money he anonymously sent the dealer's single mother who has to take care of seven children, or the talk he had (without saying what he had done) with the client's pregnant wife to see if she needed anything. This fear is secretly what drove him to become a Storm Lord, figuring the aura of the tribe would protect him somewhat. What he doesn't keep a secret, although he doesn't make a point to tell everyone, is his scepticism about that whole Moon/Wolf thing. Honestly, the entire Uratha &quot;society&quot; if you can even call it that feels a lot like a big cult. Still, that didn't really interfere with his actions among his pack (another word he has troubles with), after all, he did see what was on the other side of the gauntlet. Humans must be protected from those erratic spirits trying to cross and make a mess. Also, he's seen what the Pure were capable of, and compared to them, the Forsaken are undoubtedly the good guys.<br /> <br /> There is one way to fight fear, though. Power. Jason now runs Silver Lining Network and he's one of the richest people in Lansing, maybe Michigan. The few encounters his pack had with the Pure convinced him that the situation had to change. The current Uratha society is unfit for a war of this scale against a genocidal enemy. Unbeknownst to other werewolves, he has started to build his own network : Besides regularly dealing with the local crow spirits who make very good scouts, he is sharing information with a ranked wolfblooded FBI agent and will reveal what he is when he figures he can trust him enough. He also started looking for other unsatisfied and... interesting Forsaken to create an information network, a sort of council that could map out the territories in North America (for starters) and maybe try coordinating their actions. He's also bought a case of 50 kg of industrial grade silver granules he stored in a bank vault, just in case. Jason would hate to kill again, but if it ever comes to that, there are people against who you just don't take chances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}